      "title": "HDR playground",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "HDR / exposure-bracketing playground\n\nFour tripod exposures of the St. Louis Arch (EV -4.72 / -1.82 / +1.51 / +4.09) are stacked darkest-to-brightest into ONE image batch with core 'Batch Images'. Two HDR paths run from that batch post alignment:\n\n1. 'HDR Exposure Fusion (Mertens)' blends the best-exposed regions of every frame straight into a display-ready picture - no exposure times, no tonemapping.\n2. 'HDR Merge to Radiance' recovers the camera response from the shutter times and fuses a float RADIANCE map (values well past 1.0). It is not directly displayable, so it is shown through 'Preview CV Array' (heatmap) and compressed back to a picture by three 'HDR Tonemap' operators - Reinhard, Drago and Mantiuk - so you can compare their looks.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
